# Binary files must never go through line-ending conversion.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so on checkout Git rewrites LF to
# CRLF in anything it believes is text. It decides that by looking for a NUL
# byte in the first 8000 bytes — which works for JPEG and PNG, and fails for
# db/seed_files/penawaran-contoh.pdf, a small hand-built PDF containing no NUL
# at all. Git classified it as text.
#
# The damage is not cosmetic. A PDF's trailer points at a byte offset, and
# every xref entry is a byte offset; injecting one CR per line shifts all of
# them. Measured: a fresh clone produced 1593 bytes instead of 1547, with 46
# CR bytes added, and `startxref` pointing into the middle of a font object.
# The file opened from the repo was a broken document, while the one in the
# working tree where it was created was fine — which is the kind of bug that
# gets blamed on everything except version control.
#
# Listed by extension rather than fixed for the one file, because the next
# binary fixture will have the same problem and no warning worth reading.
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
*.doc  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xls  binary
*.zip  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.db   binary
